  "raw_text": "No. A 10% month-over-month sales decline alone doesn’t prove the campaign failed.\n\nYou’d need to compare results against:\n\n- A control group or credible no-campaign baseline\n- Seasonal and market trends\n- Campaign goals and targeted products/audiences\n- Spend, revenue, profit, and return on ad spend\n- Leads, conversions, customer acquisition, and longer sales cycles\n- Other factors such as pricing, inventory, competition, or economic changes\n\nIt’s possible sales would have fallen more without the campaign. The right conclusion is that sales declined—not necessarily that the campaign caused the decline or failed.",
